This is the brainfuck compiler.
the main() function is defined in main.c

you can include or exclude the sanity checks with assert()
by undefining the DEBUG macro in include/config.h

functions for parsing brainfuck and generating assembly
are at include/brainfuck.h
and libs/brainfuck.c for their implementations

the functions for printing the help menu and parsing command line arguments
are located at include/main_helpers.h
and libs/helpers.c for their implementations

the code that spawns child processes that assembles, and links the assembly
is located at include/compiler.h
and libs/compiler.c for their implementations

the brainfuck optimizer is located at include/brainfuck_opt.h
and libs/brainfuck_opt.c for the implementations of simple optimizers,
and libs/optimizers/ for the implementations of more complex optimizers

the resizing arrays are located at include/arrays.h
and libs/arrays.c for the implementations

I have made it somewhat simple to add your own algorithm-specific optimizers,
for an example with the square algorithm you can see
libs/optimizers/square_alg.c
after making functions to detect, and replace the algorithm with custom
assembly, you can then call them from the optimize_brainfuck() function
in the libs/brainfuck.c source file.
Remember to call purge_instructions(), collapse_instructions(),
purge_instructions() again, remove_opposite_instructions(), and
purge_instructions() again,
an auxilery helper is provided to call all of those functions,
it is called collapse_remove_and_purge()

Documentation may not be attached with the implementation of a function,
but should be attached to the declaration in the header file for the function
